        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="WOL02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Dr</roleName>
                        <forename>John</forename>
                        <surname>Wolcot</surname>
                        <addName>pseudonym Peter Pindar</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1738-05">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1819-01-14"/>
                    <occupation>poet</occupation>
                    <occupation>satirist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin sees Wolcot several times a year from 1795 until Wolcot's 
    death, with the exception of the early 1810s. </p>
                        <p>In December 1807, John Wolcot (1738-1819) was the target of a notorious court case 
     for ‘criminal conversation’ (seduction) of his landlord’s wife.  Wolcot was then seventy 
     and the case was thrown out when he pleaded that he had no fire left!  
     Godwin was on good terms with him and may have commissioned work from him before he eventually went blind in 1814.</p>
                        <p>The entries for Wolcot are consistent and 
the death-date Godwin gives is one day off from
that of the <title>DNB</title> (Godwin records it on the 13th Jan. 
1819 and the <title>DNB</title> as the 14th) </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
